On Sat, Jun 05, 2004 at 05:01:13PM -0700, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> Voting closes at ~17:00 PST tomorrow.

Or not.

As discussion is currently being made WRT a minor change to lo'i, that
seems imprudent.

Furhermore, a user who has not participated at all until now came in
mere minutes before voting was closed and registered a "No" vote.  As
voting No without an explanation is a hanging offense around here, I'm
giving that person time to explain emself.

John Cowan suggested a changing to the voting timeline that I'm inclined
to agree with, so here's how it's going to work:

Assuming that we have consensus minus one, voting on gadri closes once
24 hours passes with no changes, and no sign that the shepherd is about
to make one.

Let me know if you have a problem with that theory.

-Robin

